"Sets SASL mechanism used by authentication. Available values: ++*++ `DIGEST-SHA-512` - Uses the SHA-512 hashing algorithm to securely hash and verify credentials. This is the default. ++*++ `DIGEST-MD5` - Uses the MD5 hashing algorithm in addition to nonces to encrypt credentials. ++*++ `EXTERNAL` - Uses client certificates to provide valid identities to Infinispan Server and enable encryption. ++*++ `PLAIN` - Sends credentials in plain text (unencrypted) over the wire in a way that is similar to HTTP BASIC authentication. You should use `PLAIN` authentication only in combination with TLS encryption.\n"
"\n"
